 "mechanism": "Stat bodies are read with os.open/os.read and decoded whole with the same codec after the same default-decoder warning, in place of a text stream. Scan rows still go through identity(pid, with_namespace=False), owner lookup included, so a row whose process vanished by that lookup is dropped exactly as before. process_names() lists /proc with os.scandir on every interpreter. Per-signal full family scans, the 3 s deadline, escalation, refusals, two complete empty scans and the acknowledgement are unchanged.",
 "repair": {
  "F3": "The 80399fae lineage() reader kept a row whose process exited between its stat read and the former owner lookup; its parent edge could pull earlier-read children (after PID wrap) into the family. Restored: scan rows use identity() again. The intra-scan race differential now finds no difference in outcome, delivered signals or any descendants() result.",
  "F5": "Python-version-gated listing removed; os.scandir is compared with Path.iterdir on a stable directory (stableListing) and live /proc (listing).",
  "F1": "The earlier ack17Probe row \"a\" (source 3299de04...) was an intermediate draft, not the subject its note named. It is removed; ack17Probe below ran the subject bytes and records their digest."
 },
